## Scope and preservation

This was a Supplement-only editorial pass. No generated table, evidence artifact, checkpoint record, executable contract, support map, dense-grid output, count decomposition, margin diagnostic, or raw numerical value was removed or changed. The historical Lockbox-v1 record remains transparent and is now headed **Historical prospective-audit record and analyzer QA**. No Lockbox-v2 reference was added.

## Redundancy reductions

- Replaced repeated detector/stress-contract exposition with short pointers to the executable contract table while retaining sampling, provenance, and replay constraints.
- Shortened repeated interpretations of dataset, checkpoint, eligibility-lock, dense-grid, truncation, count-conditioning, and margin results; all supporting tables and reported estimates remain.
- Removed repeated conclusion sentences after the held-out diagnostic table and after the reduced-budget table; the values remain in the tables and the main manuscript.
- Compressed Lockbox-v1 chronology and post-access QA wording while retaining the one-shot termination, no-rerun status, formal `null` status, exploratory designation, QA test coverage, parity check, hashes, and no-verdict record.
- Retained only local technical boundaries needed to prevent misreading; repeated generic causal/treatment/universal disclaimers were not duplicated.

